{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a harness adapter runs inside a "},{"type":"link","href":"./overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sandbox"}]},{"type":"text","value":", everything it does is\nobservable on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" stream: the same AG-UI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamChunk"},{"type":"text","value":"s any "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" run\nproduces, plus namespaced "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" events for sandbox- and harness-specifics."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page is about the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stream the client reads"}]},{"type":"text","value":". To run server-side callbacks\non file changes, or to log sandbox internals, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./observability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observability"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-stream","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The stream"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A harness run produces standard AG-UI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamChunk"},{"type":"text","value":"s:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text"}]},{"type":"text","value":": incremental assistant output."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool calls"}]},{"type":"text","value":", including bridged "},{"type":"link","href":"./tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":", which surface as ordinary\ntool-call chunks the moment the in-sandbox agent invokes them."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reasoning"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the agent's thinking, where the harness exposes it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run lifecycle"}]},{"type":"text","value":": run started, run finished, and related boundaries."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"custom-events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom events"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On top of the standard chunks, the sandbox and harness layers emit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":"\nevents ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.type === 'CUSTOM'"},{"type":"text","value":"), each with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" and a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Event "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Emitted by"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-build.session-id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok Build adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"once, when the in-sandbox session is created or resumed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the resumable harness session id"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude-code.session-id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude Code adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"once, when the in-sandbox session is created or resumed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the resumable harness session id"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codex.session-id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Codex adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"once, when the session is created or resumed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the resumable harness session id"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opencode.session-id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenCode adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"once, when the session is created or resumed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the resumable harness session id"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file.changed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"harness adapter (e.g. Grok Build, Claude Code)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"after the run completes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ path: string; diff: string }"},{"type":"text","value":": the whole working-tree "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git diff"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"path"},{"type":"text","value":" is always "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'.'"},{"type":"text","value":", the tree root)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the engine, automatically"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per file create / change / delete while a sandbox is active"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'create' | 'change' | 'delete'; path: string; timestamp: number }"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file.diff"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the engine, opt-in via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileEvents: { diff: true }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per file create / change / delete, after the matching "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ path: string; diff: string }"},{"type":"text","value":": a unified patch of that one file vs the session's git baseline"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":" event lets you resume a harness session on a follow-up run\n(pass it back via the adapter's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.sessionId"},{"type":"text","value":"). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file"},{"type":"text","value":" is\nemitted automatically whenever a sandbox is active and file watching is on, with\nno hooks required. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file.diff"},{"type":"text","value":" is off by default (computing a diff on\nevery change has a cost); turn it on with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileEvents: { diff: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":" when the client needs to render the change itself, not just\nknow it happened:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\";\n\nconst repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-agent\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n  fileEvents: { diff: true }, // also emit sandbox.file.diff per change\n});","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./observability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observability"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to also handle file changes server-side\nvia hooks (which get the same diff, plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"before()"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"after()"},{"type":"text","value":"), or to turn\nthe watcher off entirely."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bridged tools emit their own events too."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" tool that runs through\nthe "},{"type":"link","href":"./tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tool bridge"}]},{"type":"text","value":" can stream "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" events back mid-execution. Code\nmode, for example, emits "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:execution_started"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:console"},{"type":"text","value":"\n(plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:external_call"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"…_result"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"…_error"},{"type":"text","value":") so you can show its\nprogress live. Read them with the same pattern below."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reading-custom-events-on-the-client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reading CUSTOM events on the client"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" event TanStack AI itself emits, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandbox.file.diff"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file.changed"},{"type":"text","value":", the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":" events, and more, has\na fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" and a concrete "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" shape, unified as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KnownCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":".\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":"'s return type narrows accordingly: check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.type === 'CUSTOM'"},{"type":"text","value":"\nand then compare "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.name"},{"type":"text","value":" to a literal string. No helper, no cast, the\nplain "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"if"},{"type":"text","value":" types "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.value"},{"type":"text","value":" for you:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { stream } from \"./my-run\";\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"sandbox.file\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.type, chunk.value.path); // typed, no cast\n  } else if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"sandbox.file.diff\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.path, chunk.value.diff); // typed, no cast\n  } else if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"file.changed\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.diff); // typed, no cast\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"session-id-events-aren-t-one-literal-name","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Session-id events aren't one literal name"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":" is emitted per-adapter ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude-code.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codex.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-build.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opencode.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":"), so its\ntype is the template-literal name "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"`${string}.session-id`"},{"type":"text","value":", not a single\nstring. If you know which adapter you're running, compare the exact literal\nit narrows "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.value"},{"type":"text","value":" the same as any other event:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { resumeSession } from \"./session\";\nimport { stream } from \"./my-run\";\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"claude-code.session-id\") {\n    resumeSession(chunk.value.sessionId); // typed as string, no cast\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.name.endsWith('.session-id')"},{"type":"text","value":" does "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" narrow."}]},{"type":"text","value":" It's a plain\nboolean expression, not something TypeScript can attach to a type, so\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.value"},{"type":"text","value":" stays whatever it was before the check (effectively\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":"), even though the check happens to be correct at runtime. If you\nneed to handle "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"any"}]},{"type":"text","value":" adapter's session id without listing every adapter's\nliteral name, write a small type predicate instead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { KnownCustomEvent, SessionIdEvent } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { resumeSession } from \"./session\";\nimport { stream } from \"./my-run\";\n\nfunction isSessionIdEvent(\n  chunk: KnownCustomEvent,\n): chunk is SessionIdEvent {\n  return chunk.name.endsWith(\".session-id\");\n}\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && isSessionIdEvent(chunk)) {\n    resumeSession(chunk.value.sessionId); // typed as string, no cast\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This predicate is something you write yourself when you need it, TanStack\nAI doesn't ship a guard API. Plain literal-"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" narrowing (as above) is\nthe primary, no-helper pattern; reach for a predicate only for this\n\"any adapter\" case."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../protocol/custom-events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Events Reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full typed\nevent taxonomy, the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatStream"},{"type":"text","value":" type this narrowing relies on, and the\ntradeoff for your own "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" calls."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-gets-stored","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What gets stored"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your user reopens a thread the next morning and wants what they saw before: the\ncommands the agent ran and what came back. The stream on this page is live output.\nThe transcript your app keeps is a different thing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wire "},{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/chat-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"chat persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":" next to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":" and a\nfinished run leaves this in the message store:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The harness produced"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the store"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes, as the assistant message."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool calls (name and arguments)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes, as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCalls"},{"type":"text","value":" on an assistant message."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool results"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes, as a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role: 'tool'"},{"type":"text","value":" message."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reasoning"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" events (file events, code-mode console, session ids)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"So reopening the thread rebuilds the tool cards with their results, on any device."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" events are not messages, so anything your UI builds from them (a file list,\na console panel) lasts only for that visit. Keep that state yourself if you want it\nback."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two limits to know about:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All of the harness's text arrives as one final assistant message. A restored thread\nreads as the tool cards in the order they ran, then the full text."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A stored result is the string the harness reported. Reopening a thread never re-runs\na tool."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"trim-what-you-keep","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trim what you keep"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To decide whether to store a transcript at all, see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/build-a-sandbox-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build a Sandbox Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":". This section is the finer knob:\nyou are storing one, and you want it smaller."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One run's tool output can be hundreds of kilobytes, and results reach your store\nwhole. Your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MessageStore"},{"type":"text","value":" decides what to keep. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isSandboxToolCall"},{"type":"text","value":" tells you which\ncalls the harness ran inside the sandbox, so you never have to know how they are\nmarked. It reads a rendered "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-call"},{"type":"text","value":" part too, which is handy for filtering a\nclient-side view."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capping each result keeps the cards and bounds the size:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { ModelMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport type { MessageStore } from \"@tanstack/ai-persistence\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\nconst MAX_RESULT = 8_000;\n\nconst store: MessageStore = {\n  async saveThread(threadId, messages) {\n    const capped = messages.map((message: ModelMessage) =>\n      message.role === \"tool\" && typeof message.content === \"string\"\n        ? { ...message, content: message.content.slice(0, MAX_RESULT) }\n        : message,\n    );\n    await db.saveThread(threadId, capped);\n  },\n  loadThread: (threadId) => db.loadThread(threadId),\n};","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To drop the history instead, remove each result with its call. A result whose call is\nmissing is worse than either, because providers reject it."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { isSandboxToolCall } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport type { ModelMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport type { MessageStore } from \"@tanstack/ai-persistence\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\nconst store: MessageStore = {\n  async saveThread(threadId, messages) {\n    const dropped = new Set<string>();\n    const kept: Array<ModelMessage> = [];\n    for (const message of messages) {\n      const calls = message.toolCalls;\n      if (calls && calls.length > 0 && calls.every(isSandboxToolCall)) {\n        for (const call of calls) dropped.add(call.id);\n        continue;\n      }\n      if (\n        message.role === \"tool\" &&\n        message.toolCallId !== undefined &&\n        dropped.has(message.toolCallId)\n      ) {\n        continue;\n      }\n      kept.push(message);\n    }\n    await db.saveThread(threadId, kept);\n  },\n  loadThread: (threadId) => db.loadThread(threadId),\n};","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dropping them is safe. They are display history, and nothing resumes from them: the\nnext turn's request to the model never carries them either, because they name tools\nthe provider was never given."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./observability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observability"}]},{"type":"text","value":", server-side file-event hooks (with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"before()"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"after()"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"diff()"},{"type":"text","value":"), debug logging, and the low-level watcher."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../protocol/custom-events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Events Reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":", the full "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KnownCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" taxonomy and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatStream"},{"type":"text","value":" type."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":", bridged host tools that surface as tool-call (and CUSTOM) chunks."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start"}]},{"type":"text","value":", read the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file.changed"},{"type":"text","value":" diff end to end."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"the-stream","text":"The stream","level":2},{"id":"custom-events","text":"Custom events","level":2},{"id":"reading-custom-events-on-the-client","text":"Reading CUSTOM events on the client","level":2},{"id":"session-id-events-aren-t-one-literal-name","text":"Session-id events aren't one literal name","level":3},{"id":"what-gets-stored","text":"What gets stored","level":2},{"id":"trim-what-you-keep","text":"Trim what you keep","level":3},{"id":"related","text":"Related","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nWhen a harness adapter runs inside a [sandbox](./overview), everything it does is\nobservable on the `chat()` stream: the same AG-UI `StreamChunk`s any `chat()` run\nproduces, plus namespaced `CUSTOM` events for sandbox- and harness-specifics.\n\nThis page is about the **stream the client reads**. To run server-side callbacks\non file changes, or to log sandbox internals, see [Observability](./observability).\n\n## The stream\n\nA harness run produces standard AG-UI `StreamChunk`s:\n\n- **Text**: incremental assistant output.\n- **Tool calls**, including bridged [tools](./tools), which surface as ordinary\n  tool-call chunks the moment the in-sandbox agent invokes them.\n- **Reasoning**: the agent's thinking, where the harness exposes it.\n- **Run lifecycle**: run started, run finished, and related boundaries.\n\n## Custom events\n\nOn top of the standard chunks, the sandbox and harness layers emit `CUSTOM`\nevents (`chunk.type === 'CUSTOM'`), each with a `name` and a `value`:\n\n| Event `name` | Emitted by | When | `value` |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `grok-build.session-id` | Grok Build adapter | once, when the in-sandbox session is created or resumed | the resumable harness session id |\n| `claude-code.session-id` | Claude Code adapter | once, when the in-sandbox session is created or resumed | the resumable harness session id |\n| `codex.session-id` | Codex adapter | once, when the session is created or resumed | the resumable harness session id |\n| `opencode.session-id` | OpenCode adapter | once, when the session is created or resumed | the resumable harness session id |\n| `file.changed` | harness adapter (e.g. Grok Build, Claude Code) | after the run completes | `{ path: string; diff: string }`: the whole working-tree `git diff` (`path` is always `'.'`, the tree root) |\n| `sandbox.file` | the engine, automatically | per file create / change / delete while a sandbox is active | `{ type: 'create' \\| 'change' \\| 'delete'; path: string; timestamp: number }` |\n| `sandbox.file.diff` | the engine, opt-in via `fileEvents: { diff: true }` | per file create / change / delete, after the matching `sandbox.file` | `{ path: string; diff: string }`: a unified patch of that one file vs the session's git baseline |\n\nThe `*.session-id` event lets you resume a harness session on a follow-up run\n(pass it back via the adapter's `modelOptions.sessionId`). `sandbox.file` is\nemitted automatically whenever a sandbox is active and file watching is on, with\nno hooks required. `sandbox.file.diff` is off by default (computing a diff on\nevery change has a cost); turn it on with `fileEvents: { diff: true }` on\n`defineSandbox` when the client needs to render the change itself, not just\nknow it happened:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\";\n\nconst repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-agent\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n  fileEvents: { diff: true }, // also emit sandbox.file.diff per change\n});\n```\n\nSee [Observability](./observability) to also handle file changes server-side\nvia hooks (which get the same diff, plus `before()`/`after()`), or to turn\nthe watcher off entirely.\n\n> **Bridged tools emit their own events too.** A `chat()` tool that runs through\n> the [tool bridge](./tools) can stream `CUSTOM` events back mid-execution. Code\n> mode, for example, emits `code_mode:execution_started` and `code_mode:console`\n> (plus `code_mode:external_call` / `…_result` / `…_error`) so you can show its\n> progress live. Read them with the same pattern below.\n\n## Reading CUSTOM events on the client\n\nEvery `CUSTOM` event TanStack AI itself emits, `sandbox.file`,\n`sandbox.file.diff`, `file.changed`, the `*.session-id` events, and more, has\na fixed `name` and a concrete `value` shape, unified as `KnownCustomEvent`.\n`chat()`'s return type narrows accordingly: check `chunk.type === 'CUSTOM'`\nand then compare `chunk.name` to a literal string. No helper, no cast, the\nplain `if` types `chunk.value` for you:\n\n```ts\nimport { stream } from \"./my-run\";\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"sandbox.file\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.type, chunk.value.path); // typed, no cast\n  } else if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"sandbox.file.diff\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.path, chunk.value.diff); // typed, no cast\n  } else if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"file.changed\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.diff); // typed, no cast\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Session-id events aren't one literal name\n\n`*.session-id` is emitted per-adapter (`claude-code.session-id`,\n`codex.session-id`, `grok-build.session-id`, `opencode.session-id`), so its\ntype is the template-literal name `` `${string}.session-id` ``, not a single\nstring. If you know which adapter you're running, compare the exact literal\nit narrows `chunk.value` the same as any other event:\n\n```ts\nimport { resumeSession } from \"./session\";\nimport { stream } from \"./my-run\";\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"claude-code.session-id\") {\n    resumeSession(chunk.value.sessionId); // typed as string, no cast\n  }\n}\n```\n\n> **`chunk.name.endsWith('.session-id')` does *not* narrow.** It's a plain\n> boolean expression, not something TypeScript can attach to a type, so\n> `chunk.value` stays whatever it was before the check (effectively\n> `unknown`), even though the check happens to be correct at runtime. If you\n> need to handle *any* adapter's session id without listing every adapter's\n> literal name, write a small type predicate instead:\n>\n> ```ts\n> import type { KnownCustomEvent, SessionIdEvent } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n> import { resumeSession } from \"./session\";\n> import { stream } from \"./my-run\";\n>\n> function isSessionIdEvent(\n>   chunk: KnownCustomEvent,\n> ): chunk is SessionIdEvent {\n>   return chunk.name.endsWith(\".session-id\");\n> }\n>\n> for await (const chunk of stream) {\n>   if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && isSessionIdEvent(chunk)) {\n>     resumeSession(chunk.value.sessionId); // typed as string, no cast\n>   }\n> }\n> ```\n>\n> This predicate is something you write yourself when you need it, TanStack\n> AI doesn't ship a guard API. Plain literal-`name` narrowing (as above) is\n> the primary, no-helper pattern; reach for a predicate only for this\n> \"any adapter\" case.\n\nSee [Custom Events Reference](../protocol/custom-events) for the full typed\nevent taxonomy, the `ChatStream` type this narrowing relies on, and the\ntradeoff for your own `emitCustomEvent` calls.\n\n## What gets stored\n\nYour user reopens a thread the next morning and wants what they saw before: the\ncommands the agent ran and what came back. The stream on this page is live output.\nThe transcript your app keeps is a different thing.\n\nWire [chat persistence](../persistence/chat-persistence) next to `withSandbox` and a\nfinished run leaves this in the message store:\n\n| The harness produced | In the store |\n| --- | --- |\n| Text | Yes, as the assistant message. |\n| Tool calls (name and arguments) | Yes, as `toolCalls` on an assistant message. |\n| Tool results | Yes, as a `role: 'tool'` message. |\n| Reasoning | No. |\n| `CUSTOM` events (file events, code-mode console, session ids) | No. |\n\nSo reopening the thread rebuilds the tool cards with their results, on any device.\n\n`CUSTOM` events are not messages, so anything your UI builds from them (a file list,\na console panel) lasts only for that visit. Keep that state yourself if you want it\nback.\n\nTwo limits to know about:\n\n- All of the harness's text arrives as one final assistant message. A restored thread\n  reads as the tool cards in the order they ran, then the full text.\n- A stored result is the string the harness reported. Reopening a thread never re-runs\n  a tool.\n\n### Trim what you keep\n\nTo decide whether to store a transcript at all, see\n[Build a Sandbox Adapter](../persistence/build-a-sandbox-adapter). This section is the finer knob:\nyou are storing one, and you want it smaller.\n\nOne run's tool output can be hundreds of kilobytes, and results reach your store\nwhole. Your `MessageStore` decides what to keep. `isSandboxToolCall` tells you which\ncalls the harness ran inside the sandbox, so you never have to know how they are\nmarked. It reads a rendered `tool-call` part too, which is handy for filtering a\nclient-side view.\n\nCapping each result keeps the cards and bounds the size:\n\n```ts\nimport type { ModelMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport type { MessageStore } from \"@tanstack/ai-persistence\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\nconst MAX_RESULT = 8_000;\n\nconst store: MessageStore = {\n  async saveThread(threadId, messages) {\n    const capped = messages.map((message: ModelMessage) =>\n      message.role === \"tool\" && typeof message.content === \"string\"\n        ? { ...message, content: message.content.slice(0, MAX_RESULT) }\n        : message,\n    );\n    await db.saveThread(threadId, capped);\n  },\n  loadThread: (threadId) => db.loadThread(threadId),\n};\n```\n\nTo drop the history instead, remove each result with its call. A result whose call is\nmissing is worse than either, because providers reject it.\n\n```ts\nimport { isSandboxToolCall } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport type { ModelMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport type { MessageStore } from \"@tanstack/ai-persistence\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\nconst store: MessageStore = {\n  async saveThread(threadId, messages) {\n    const dropped = new Set<string>();\n    const kept: Array<ModelMessage> = [];\n    for (const message of messages) {\n      const calls = message.toolCalls;\n      if (calls && calls.length > 0 && calls.every(isSandboxToolCall)) {\n        for (const call of calls) dropped.add(call.id);\n        continue;\n      }\n      if (\n        message.role === \"tool\" &&\n        message.toolCallId !== undefined &&\n        dropped.has(message.toolCallId)\n      ) {\n        continue;\n      }\n      kept.push(message);\n    }\n    await db.saveThread(threadId, kept);\n  },\n  loadThread: (threadId) => db.loadThread(threadId),\n};\n```\n\nDropping them is safe. They are display history, and nothing resumes from them: the\nnext turn's request to the model never carries them either, because they name tools\nthe provider was never given.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Observability](./observability), server-side file-event hooks (with `before()`/`after()`/`diff()`), debug logging, and the low-level watcher.\n- [Custom Events Reference](../protocol/custom-events), the full `KnownCustomEvent` taxonomy and the `ChatStream` type.\n- [Tools](./tools), bridged host tools that surface as tool-call (and CUSTOM) chunks.\n- [Quick Start](./quick-start), read the `file.changed` diff end to end.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Events\nid: events\norder: 9\ndescription: \"Everything a harness agent does inside a sandbox (text, tool calls, reasoning, session ids, and file edits) streams back as AG-UI chunks plus namespaced CUSTOM events.\"\n---\n\nWhen a harness adapter runs inside a [sandbox](./overview), everything it does is\nobservable on the `chat()` stream: the same AG-UI `StreamChunk`s any `chat()` run\nproduces, plus namespaced `CUSTOM` events for sandbox- and harness-specifics.\n\nThis page is about the **stream the client reads**. To run server-side callbacks\non file changes, or to log sandbox internals, see [Observability](./observability).\n\n## The stream\n\nA harness run produces standard AG-UI `StreamChunk`s:\n\n- **Text**: incremental assistant output.\n- **Tool calls**, including bridged [tools](./tools), which surface as ordinary\n  tool-call chunks the moment the in-sandbox agent invokes them.\n- **Reasoning**: the agent's thinking, where the harness exposes it.\n- **Run lifecycle**: run started, run finished, and related boundaries.\n\n## Custom events\n\nOn top of the standard chunks, the sandbox and harness layers emit `CUSTOM`\nevents (`chunk.type === 'CUSTOM'`), each with a `name` and a `value`:\n\n| Event `name` | Emitted by | When | `value` |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `grok-build.session-id` | Grok Build adapter | once, when the in-sandbox session is created or resumed | the resumable harness session id |\n| `claude-code.session-id` | Claude Code adapter | once, when the in-sandbox session is created or resumed | the resumable harness session id |\n| `codex.session-id` | Codex adapter | once, when the session is created or resumed | the resumable harness session id |\n| `opencode.session-id` | OpenCode adapter | once, when the session is created or resumed | the resumable harness session id |\n| `file.changed` | harness adapter (e.g. Grok Build, Claude Code) | after the run completes | `{ path: string; diff: string }`: the whole working-tree `git diff` (`path` is always `'.'`, the tree root) |\n| `sandbox.file` | the engine, automatically | per file create / change / delete while a sandbox is active | `{ type: 'create' \\| 'change' \\| 'delete'; path: string; timestamp: number }` |\n| `sandbox.file.diff` | the engine, opt-in via `fileEvents: { diff: true }` | per file create / change / delete, after the matching `sandbox.file` | `{ path: string; diff: string }`: a unified patch of that one file vs the session's git baseline |\n\nThe `*.session-id` event lets you resume a harness session on a follow-up run\n(pass it back via the adapter's `modelOptions.sessionId`). `sandbox.file` is\nemitted automatically whenever a sandbox is active and file watching is on, with\nno hooks required. `sandbox.file.diff` is off by default (computing a diff on\nevery change has a cost); turn it on with `fileEvents: { diff: true }` on\n`defineSandbox` when the client needs to render the change itself, not just\nknow it happened:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\";\n\nconst repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-agent\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n  fileEvents: { diff: true }, // also emit sandbox.file.diff per change\n});\n```\n\nSee [Observability](./observability) to also handle file changes server-side\nvia hooks (which get the same diff, plus `before()`/`after()`), or to turn\nthe watcher off entirely.\n\n> **Bridged tools emit their own events too.** A `chat()` tool that runs through\n> the [tool bridge](./tools) can stream `CUSTOM` events back mid-execution. Code\n> mode, for example, emits `code_mode:execution_started` and `code_mode:console`\n> (plus `code_mode:external_call` / `…_result` / `…_error`) so you can show its\n> progress live. Read them with the same pattern below.\n\n## Reading CUSTOM events on the client\n\nEvery `CUSTOM` event TanStack AI itself emits, `sandbox.file`,\n`sandbox.file.diff`, `file.changed`, the `*.session-id` events, and more, has\na fixed `name` and a concrete `value` shape, unified as `KnownCustomEvent`.\n`chat()`'s return type narrows accordingly: check `chunk.type === 'CUSTOM'`\nand then compare `chunk.name` to a literal string. No helper, no cast, the\nplain `if` types `chunk.value` for you:\n\n```ts\nimport { stream } from \"./my-run\";\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"sandbox.file\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.type, chunk.value.path); // typed, no cast\n  } else if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"sandbox.file.diff\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.path, chunk.value.diff); // typed, no cast\n  } else if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"file.changed\") {\n    console.log(chunk.value.diff); // typed, no cast\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Session-id events aren't one literal name\n\n`*.session-id` is emitted per-adapter (`claude-code.session-id`,\n`codex.session-id`, `grok-build.session-id`, `opencode.session-id`), so its\ntype is the template-literal name `` `${string}.session-id` ``, not a single\nstring. If you know which adapter you're running, compare the exact literal\nit narrows `chunk.value` the same as any other event:\n\n```ts\nimport { resumeSession } from \"./session\";\nimport { stream } from \"./my-run\";\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && chunk.name === \"claude-code.session-id\") {\n    resumeSession(chunk.value.sessionId); // typed as string, no cast\n  }\n}\n```\n\n> **`chunk.name.endsWith('.session-id')` does *not* narrow.** It's a plain\n> boolean expression, not something TypeScript can attach to a type, so\n> `chunk.value` stays whatever it was before the check (effectively\n> `unknown`), even though the check happens to be correct at runtime. If you\n> need to handle *any* adapter's session id without listing every adapter's\n> literal name, write a small type predicate instead:\n>\n> ```ts\n> import type { KnownCustomEvent, SessionIdEvent } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n> import { resumeSession } from \"./session\";\n> import { stream } from \"./my-run\";\n>\n> function isSessionIdEvent(\n>   chunk: KnownCustomEvent,\n> ): chunk is SessionIdEvent {\n>   return chunk.name.endsWith(\".session-id\");\n> }\n>\n> for await (const chunk of stream) {\n>   if (chunk.type === \"CUSTOM\" && isSessionIdEvent(chunk)) {\n>     resumeSession(chunk.value.sessionId); // typed as string, no cast\n>   }\n> }\n> ```\n>\n> This predicate is something you write yourself when you need it, TanStack\n> AI doesn't ship a guard API. Plain literal-`name` narrowing (as above) is\n> the primary, no-helper pattern; reach for a predicate only for this\n> \"any adapter\" case.\n\nSee [Custom Events Reference](../protocol/custom-events) for the full typed\nevent taxonomy, the `ChatStream` type this narrowing relies on, and the\ntradeoff for your own `emitCustomEvent` calls.\n\n## What gets stored\n\nYour user reopens a thread the next morning and wants what they saw before: the\ncommands the agent ran and what came back. The stream on this page is live output.\nThe transcript your app keeps is a different thing.\n\nWire [chat persistence](../persistence/chat-persistence) next to `withSandbox` and a\nfinished run leaves this in the message store:\n\n| The harness produced | In the store |\n| --- | --- |\n| Text | Yes, as the assistant message. |\n| Tool calls (name and arguments) | Yes, as `toolCalls` on an assistant message. |\n| Tool results | Yes, as a `role: 'tool'` message. |\n| Reasoning | No. |\n| `CUSTOM` events (file events, code-mode console, session ids) | No. |\n\nSo reopening the thread rebuilds the tool cards with their results, on any device.\n\n`CUSTOM` events are not messages, so anything your UI builds from them (a file list,\na console panel) lasts only for that visit. Keep that state yourself if you want it\nback.\n\nTwo limits to know about:\n\n- All of the harness's text arrives as one final assistant message. A restored thread\n  reads as the tool cards in the order they ran, then the full text.\n- A stored result is the string the harness reported. Reopening a thread never re-runs\n  a tool.\n\n### Trim what you keep\n\nTo decide whether to store a transcript at all, see\n[Build a Sandbox Adapter](../persistence/build-a-sandbox-adapter). This section is the finer knob:\nyou are storing one, and you want it smaller.\n\nOne run's tool output can be hundreds of kilobytes, and results reach your store\nwhole. Your `MessageStore` decides what to keep. `isSandboxToolCall` tells you which\ncalls the harness ran inside the sandbox, so you never have to know how they are\nmarked. It reads a rendered `tool-call` part too, which is handy for filtering a\nclient-side view.\n\nCapping each result keeps the cards and bounds the size:\n\n```ts\nimport type { ModelMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport type { MessageStore } from \"@tanstack/ai-persistence\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\nconst MAX_RESULT = 8_000;\n\nconst store: MessageStore = {\n  async saveThread(threadId, messages) {\n    const capped = messages.map((message: ModelMessage) =>\n      message.role === \"tool\" && typeof message.content === \"string\"\n        ? { ...message, content: message.content.slice(0, MAX_RESULT) }\n        : message,\n    );\n    await db.saveThread(threadId, capped);\n  },\n  loadThread: (threadId) => db.loadThread(threadId),\n};\n```\n\nTo drop the history instead, remove each result with its call. A result whose call is\nmissing is worse than either, because providers reject it.\n\n```ts\nimport { isSandboxToolCall } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport type { ModelMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport type { MessageStore } from \"@tanstack/ai-persistence\";\nimport { db } from \"./db\";\n\nconst store: MessageStore = {\n  async saveThread(threadId, messages) {\n    const dropped = new Set<string>();\n    const kept: Array<ModelMessage> = [];\n    for (const message of messages) {\n      const calls = message.toolCalls;\n      if (calls && calls.length > 0 && calls.every(isSandboxToolCall)) {\n        for (const call of calls) dropped.add(call.id);\n        continue;\n      }\n      if (\n        message.role === \"tool\" &&\n        message.toolCallId !== undefined &&\n        dropped.has(message.toolCallId)\n      ) {\n        continue;\n      }\n      kept.push(message);\n    }\n    await db.saveThread(threadId, kept);\n  },\n  loadThread: (threadId) => db.loadThread(threadId),\n};\n```\n\nDropping them is safe. They are display history, and nothing resumes from them: the\nnext turn's request to the model never carries them either, because they name tools\nthe provider was never given.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Observability](./observability), server-side file-event hooks (with `before()`/`after()`/`diff()`), debug logging, and the low-level watcher.\n- [Custom Events Reference](../protocol/custom-events), the full `KnownCustomEvent` taxonomy and the `ChatStream` type.\n- [Tools](./tools), bridged host tools that surface as tool-call (and CUSTOM) chunks.\n- [Quick Start](./quick-start), read the `file.changed` diff end to end.\n"}
